+---
+id: task-004-hourly-rental-prices
+type: task
+title: "Hourly rental prices"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Hourly rental prices
+
+## Request
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today the desk has to turn them away. Customers
+must be able to rent by the hour.
+
+`addEquipment` now also accepts an `hourlyPrice`, what one hour of rental costs. A rental shorter than a
+day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each hour. An item without
+an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+## Choices made for this request
+
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional on `Equipment`, in integer euro cents, validated like `dailyPrice`: a
+  non-negative safe integer when present. An item without it is rentable by the day only.
+- A rental is "shorter than a day" when `end - start` is less than 24 hours. Such a rental must start and
+  end on a whole UTC hour, written as ISO-8601 (`2026-06-01T09:00:00Z`; `.000` milliseconds accepted). Its
+  total is `hourlyPrice * hours`. Integer arithmetic, no discount (the long-stay discount counts days).
+- A rental of 24 hours or more keeps the existing rule: start and end at midnight UTC, priced by days. So a
+  period of exactly 24 hours is one day at the daily price, never hourly.
+- A rental shorter than a day that crosses midnight is allowed (22:00 to 02:00 is 4 hours).
+- An hourly rental of an item without `hourlyPrice` is refused by `quote` and `book`, with an error.
+- `availability` accepts hourly periods. For an hourly period it lists only items that have an hourly price,
+  so that it never offers an item `book` would refuse. Overlap is still checked on exact times, so an hourly
+  booking and a daily booking conflict only where they overlap.
+- Changes school rule 3 (below) for sub-day rentals only; daily rentals are unchanged.
+- `Quote`, `Booking` and the function signatures do not change.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC21: `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`; a non-integer or negative value is refused.
+- AC22: A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on a whole UTC hour is priced at `hourlyPrice`
+  times the number of hours (for example 09:00 to 12:00 is 3 hours).
+- AC23: A rental shorter than a day that crosses midnight is priced by its hours (22:00 to 02:00 is 4 hours).
+- AC24: `quote` and `book` refuse an hourly rental of an item without an hourly price.
+- AC25: A rental shorter than a day that does not start and end on a whole hour is refused (for example
+  09:30 to 10:30).
+- AC26: A period of 24 hours or more must still start and end at midnight UTC; a period of exactly 24 hours
+  from midnight to midnight is priced at the daily price.
+- AC27: `book` refuses an hourly period that overlaps an existing booking, allows back-to-back hourly
+  periods, and a refused booking does not change state.
+- AC28: `availability` for an hourly period lists only items with an hourly price that are free for the
+  whole hour window, and excludes an item booked for an overlapping hour.
+
+## School rules (apply)
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC, except a rental shorter than a day, which
+   covers whole hours (this request).
+4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Feature: rental module (booking desk). Story: visitors can rent a board or sail by the hour.
+Requirements: school rules 1, 2, 4 and the hourly form of rule 3; extends the pricing of task-001 (AC2, AC5)
+and the availability of task-002 (AC12) for hourly periods. Tests cover AC21–AC28 with happy and error paths.
